            <ArticleTitle>Predictors of rapid QRS widening in patients with coronary artery disease and left ventricular dysfunction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1410-2, A9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To assess the predictors of rapid QRS widening in patients with chronic ischemic left ventricular dysfunction, 82 patients who underwent &gt; or =2 electrocardiograms and exercise Doppler echocardiography were studied. In a multivariate analysis, left ventricular end-diastolic volume, a large increase in mitral regurgitant volume during exercise, and diabetes emerged as independent predictors of QRS widening.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
